{title: Forever Reign}
{artist: Hillsong Worship}
{key: C}
{tempo: 83}
{meta: cant_key C}

{comment: Intro}
[C]

{comment: VERSE 1}
You are [C]good,  You are good when there’s nothing good in me
You are [G/B]love,   You are love on display for all to see
You are [C]light,  You are light  when the darkness closes in
You are [G/B]hope, You are hope You have covered all my sin   [C]

You are [C]peace,   You are peace  when my fear is crippling
You are [G/B]true,   You are true even in my wandering
You are [C]joy,   You are joy  You’re the reason that I sing
You are [G/B]life,  You are life even death has lost it’s sting   [C]

{comment: CHORUS}
[C]Oh  I’ll run into Your [Cmaj7]arms   I’ll run into Your [Am]arms  The riches of Your love [A2]will [G]always be [Fmaj7add2]enough
Nothing [Am]compares to [G]Your embrace   [Fmaj7add2]Light of the world [Am]forever [G]reign  [Fmaj7add2]

{comment: VERSE 2}
You are [C]more,  You are more than my words will ever say
You are [G/B]Lord,  You are Lord  All creation will proclaim
You are [C]here,  You are here  In Your presence I’m made whole
You are [G/B]God, You are God  of all else I’m letting go

{comment: Bridge}

[Am]    My heart will sing [Fmaj7add2]   no other name       [C]Jesus     [G]Jesus
[Am]    My heart will sing [Fmaj7add2]   no other name       [C]Jesus     [G]Jesus   [Fmaj7add2]

